          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-105167",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1} \\\\ -3{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-7{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}3{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}-7{x}_{2} &=-9 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the first and the second equations we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{2} & =-6 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+5(3) & =3 \\\\ -3{x}_{1} & =-12 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the third equation and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ (4)-(3) & =1 \\\\ 1 & =1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=4$ and ${x}_{2}=3,$ which means\n\n$$\n4{a}_{1}+3{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=4+3=7.\n$$"
