          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-73951",
          ":question/problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{c}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{c}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,d=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}?$\n.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "If ${x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}=d,$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ \\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -11 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=-11 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAdding the second and the third  equations we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1} & =-16\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{1}=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ into the third equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-2)+{x}_{2} &=-5\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{2}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting ${x}_{1}=-2$ and ${x}_{2}=3$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} & =3 \\\\ (-2)+2(3) & =3 \\\\ 4 & =3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a false statement. \n\nSo, the system has no solution."
